The GitHub API resolves refs/tags/v1.37.1 to tag object d2b770f4c94636a992534a8d3156b6b2d8e82ac3, which points to commit f78e722310e50bcaca9276be22276d9e91d91308.

probes:
check_closure, 25 probes.
Refused:
- effect gate mustBePresent true;
- Group-kind writer under PROFILE;
- system:masters with a different holder, or with derivation BOOTSTRAP;
- kube-proxy mustBePresent true;
- a closure SA with a different holder;
- replicaset entry removed;
- SA default/replicaset-controller;
- Group system:authenticated under BOOTSTRAP;
- an unknown derivation;
- system:apiserver as NODE_AUTHORIZER, and system:nodes as PROFILE;
- writer grants in reversed order, writer resourceNames reordered, writer verb '*';
- kubelet client under BOOTSTRAP;
- mustBePresent 0;
- scheduler with pods create;
- a User named like an SA.
A bootstrap file without referencedRoles gives KeyError.
Accepted, harmless: an extra allowed-controller SA with no grants, and an arbitrary 'scopes' value (the model does not use it). A bootstrap role and a closure widened identically are also accepted, because input integrity rests on the fixture digests.

check_rbac_snapshot.
Refused:
- writer: escalate at CLUSTER, bind on clusterroles, namespaces delete/finalize/status, deletecollection on roles, MAP create;
- kubelet client: nodes/checkpoint;
- unknown subjects with impersonate:arbitrary-node, '*/token', CSR approval, VAP status, or get on pods/exec in the qualification namespace;
- Group system:serviceaccounts:kube-system with pods create;
- the absent certificate-controller with token create;
- an absent non-controller kube-system SA with pods/exec;
- a dormant account marked present;
- a system namespace or the placeholder as the qualification namespace;
- an uppercase scope, and an extra rule key.
Accepted, correctly:
- the writer's named escalate via apiGroups '*', and a namespaced VAP grant (both within its grants);
- 'nodes/*', which matches no subresource, as upstream;
- the absent namespace-controller with its own grants;
- extra rules on system:masters.
Accepted and reported:
- non-policy rules on User system:apiserver (N2);
- pods create in default, and persistentvolumes create (N6);
- configmaps update and secrets read in kube-system, nodes/status, nodes/statusz, configz and pods, and pods/portforward in kube-system (unclassified, as in round 1).

check_evidence.
Refused:
- executable paths with a trailing slash, '//', '..', or no leading '/';
- an uppercase digest, a shared artifactDigest, a wrong label;
- members 1.0; a unix URL with a query; securePort True;
- verificationKeys True or 0; issuer ' x'; signingEndpoint ''; lookup 1;
- externalAuthenticators None; staticTokenFile ''; trustedCaPrivateKeys False; bootstrapTokens 0.0;
- a duplicate plugin or AlwaysDeny; duplicate or '*' controllers;
- staticPodURL '' and staticPodURLHeader None; readOnlyPort 0.0;
- emulatedVersion '1.37'; an extra or missing featureGates component; runtimeConfig None;
- a duplicate API client; an unknown sealed token; a stale proxy configuration in a six-key profile; duplicate auto-apply paths;
- kubernetesVersion '1.37.1'; a license list;
- an implementationId of 129 characters or with a newline.
Accepted, valid under W02g:
- a '...' path segment;
- bindAddress 127.0.0.2 and ::ffff:127.0.0.1 (both loopback);
- OwnerReferencesPermissionEnforcement;
- empty apiClients;
- GATED_OFF or off-by-default controllers listed as running (a record inconsistency only).
Accepted and reported in N1 and N3:
- production with distribution name 'Unit-Distribution', or a renamed implementationId over the fixture components;
- A05's six-key fixture backend;
- backend rows with extra or invalid cgroupPath, apiIdentities or filePaths;
- nested or shared cgroupPath.
